Concern: `moved = (src[0] < 100)` in the ==0 arm — src[0] known 0 there; GCC may FOLD to constant 1 (li v0,1)! Retail has sltiu producing it (shared with the >=100 test). If GCC folds, encoding differs (li vs sltiu) BUT placement might differ too. To prevent folding, compute the flag ONCE before the if:

```c
